    "Seated foreground man | Initially visible as hands with blue jacket sleeves and white cuffs; revealed face has short side-parted dark hair, glasses, trimmed beard and moustache, medium build, blue suit, white shirt, red tie and yellow pocket square | Same visible face, hair, build, clothing and glasses at 00:09.75 | One continuous moving shot: hands enter from screen left at 00:00; torso and face emerge on the left at 00:04.50, become frontal near screen center at 00:06–00:07.75, then shift to screen right in three-quarter/profile view at 00:08–00:09.75 as the camera moves. Remains seated facing inward and looking down, with continuous arm movements. Background observers remain farther from the camera; no supported identity, placement or movement discontinuity.",
    "Light-shirted background observer | Blurred dark-haired person in a pale gray top, seated in the distance and generally facing the foreground activity | Last clearly distinguishable around 00:05.50, still seated in pale clothing | Initially left of the dark-shirted standing observer; shifts toward screen right during the camera movement and leaves the framing. Face, accessories and fine identity details are unresolved; no evidenced unexplained transition.",
    "Early dark-shirted background observer | Blurred person in a dark short-sleeved top, upright behind the foreground activity, with an arm bent toward the chest | Remains dark-clothed and upright while moving toward the right edge of the framing by approximately 00:05 | Initially screen right of the pale-shirted seated observer. Apparent screen displacement accompanies the continuous camera movement; no evidenced teleportation or identity change.",
    "Later dark-clothed background observer | Dim, blurred upright figure first distinguishable near the far left around 00:07, with an arm bent in front of the torso | Dark-clothed figure visible behind and to screen right of the foreground man near 00:09.75 | Progresses from the left background toward occlusion behind the foreground man as the camera moves, then is visible at the right. Insufficient facial or clothing detail to establish whether this is the earlier dark-shirted observer; no supported continuity violation."
